@startuml integration-recovery-sequence
' Proposed interaction, not evidence that vendor APIs have been qualified.
!include ../../../../../tooling/styles/plantuml/interaction/sequence-diagram-style.iuml
title Findings Intake - Idempotency and Recovery

actor "Scanner" as Scanner
participant "Ingest Validator" as Intake
participant "Evidence Vault" as Vault
participant "Findings Registry" as Findings
participant "GLPI or iTop" as CMDB
participant "Taiga" as Taiga
participant "Eramba" as GRC

Scanner -> Intake: signed scan event and source run ID
Intake -> Vault: store source payload and hash
Intake -> Findings: validated event and idempotency key
Findings -> CMDB: scoped asset and service lookup
CMDB --> Findings: authoritative ID or unresolved
alt authoritative record resolved
  Findings -> Taiga: upsert remediation using finding ID
  Taiga --> Findings: task ID and acknowledgement
  Findings -> GRC: risk and control evidence reference
  GRC --> Findings: decision reference
else match conflict or API failure
  Findings -> Findings: quarantine or bounded retry
end
note over Findings, Taiga
  Replay does not create duplicate remediation tasks.
end note
@enduml
